Game of Life on sparse tiles run by several places with a directory
(benchmarks/life/life-places.m) on the machine's GPU: each place is a GPU
process with a share of the GPU's teams, and the directory moves tiles
between them. The population, checksum, tiles moved and
active tiles are life-sparse.m's for the same world, for any number of
places (life-places.test), with the default world too, 8192 cells square, a
soup of 256 and 1000 steps. What the places held is all freed when they
end, and a place whose pool runs out ends the program with status 1.

The places run in GPU processes' stack of 1536 bytes a lane, as their code
runs on their lanes alone, with its values in scalar registers
(Lowering.cpp, MarkProcessCodeSingleLane).
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-places.m -o %t
RUN: %gpu-env LIFE_PLACES=2 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A
A: Population: 562
A-NEXT: Checksum: 17668223
A-NEXT: Active tiles: 36 at most, 32 at the end
A-NEXT: Tiles moved: 3
RUN: %gpu-env LIFE_PLACES=3 LIFE_WORLD=200 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=37 LIFE_STEPS=120 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
ODD: Population: 157
ODD-NEXT: Checksum: 2963654
ODD-NEXT: Active tiles: {{.*}}
ODD-NEXT: Tiles moved: 30
RUN: %gpu-env LIFE_PLACES=4 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=256 LIFE_STEPS=100 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WHOLE
WHOLE: Population: 4947
WHOLE-NEXT: Checksum: 158368224
WHOLE-NEXT: Active tiles: 1024 at most, 856 at the end
WHOLE-NEXT: Tiles moved: 161
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 LIFE_PLACES=2 timeout -k 1 120 %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DEFAULT
DEFAULT: World: 8192 x 8192 cells, tiles of 64 x 64, 8192 in each place's pool
DEFAULT: Population: 3719
DEFAULT-NEXT: Checksum: 124925383998
DEFAULT-NEXT: Active tiles: 45 at most, 43 at the end
DEFAULT-NEXT: Tiles moved: 15
DEFAULT: Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 LIFE_PLACES=2 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=256 LIFE_STEPS=10 LIFE_CAPACITY=100 not timeout -k 1 60 %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FULL
FULL: A place's pool ran out of tiles: raise LIFE_CAPACITY.
FULL-NEXT: Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated

Without -fopenmp each place runs the loops on its own lane.
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-places.m -o %t.sequential
RUN: %gpu-env LIFE_PLACES=2 LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 timeout -k 1 60 %t.sequential | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A
